                "firstName": "James C.",
                "lastName": "Lin"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "While there are new, next-generation network roll-outs due this year, projected cellular mobile phone shipments from major makers continue to show a slow-down in growth. When these companies rebound, more wireless systems are likely to come online, each with its own network of base stations. This would extend the trends for the future, which look much the same as before the stall in the current product cycle, except that economic, public relations, and regulatory interests would likely lead to co-location of towers and antennas (i.e., locating base stations from different services on the same site or structure.)",
